# Every text file is LF in the index and LF in the working tree, on every
# platform. Without this, a Windows checkout with the common `core.autocrlf=true`
# gets CRLF working copies of files that are LF in git, and `prettier --check`
# (endOfLine: "lf" in .prettierrc.yaml) then reports every file in the
# repository as misformatted, which blocks the pre-push gate.
#
# Adding this file does not convert a checkout that already exists -- git only
# rewrites working copies on checkout. See "Line endings" in the README for the
# one-time migration.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces. `text=auto` already detects these by their NUL bytes, but an
# archive or a font that happens to have none would be mangled as text.
*.tgz binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary

# cmd.exe needs CRLF: with LF it mis-seeks on `goto` and labels. There are no
# such files here today; this keeps the first one that arrives from breaking.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
